\tag{fdip}
\title{Ginsparg–Wilson operators}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{A positive Wilson coefficient lifts the zero blocks of the free
centered operator at nonzero sampled corners (\ref{fdip-0144}).
In even dimension the Wilson term also breaks anticommutation
with the volume grading #{C}.
The quadratic relation
#{C\mathcal D+\mathcal D C=a\mathcal D C\mathcal D} of
\ref{fdip-009X} modifies that condition. Which grading still
acts on the zero modes, and how can one construct a finite
operator satisfying the relation?}

\p{A self-adjoint grading on a finite-dimensional complex Hilbert
space is enough to pose these questions. For a translation-invariant
free symbol on the periodic grid with a site-independent grading,
they apply to each Fourier block.}
